# metallica_spike 1.04 - drafted by port_tool.py from metallica_spike-1.03.port (PAD-306): every
# function and global placed in this build's own program; switches, callouts, scenes and values
# copied from 1.03. This build numbers its bus events from 0x46 up one higher than 1.03 (ids end
# at 207); its event lines below were measured here (PAD-306).
# program sha1 db62753b2f8a70806633d08f0faf4f306221ac55.
# Emulator-proven 2026-10-01 by a Try it on the stock 1.04 card (rig slot 3, muted): the runtime
# armed with this port (callout screens clips own-sound multiball), a game started, the mode's
# start shot (Grave tgt-left, switch 46) started the mode, its title clip played full screen in
# the Video grafted into the HUD, its own screen showed over the HUD for the 30 s and was hidden
# 6 s after the clock ran out.
# Emulator-proven 2026-10-01 by a full build check (modes/gamecheck.sh play full, PAD-306, rig slot
# 2): 35 of its 40 shots came from their switches, a drain ended each ball, and the 7 events below
# fired where their names say (a tilted ball, three balls to the game's end). Shots no press made
# (their switch is left out of the check, or needs two): Left outlane, Right outlane, Coffin lock 1,
# Coffin lock 2, Coffin lock 3. A stack no mode was seen held back by a multiball and by a song mode's
# live record (PAD-306, rig slot 2).
# Also proven 2026-10-01 (PAD-306, rig slot 3): Check this game - 37 of its 40 switch lines gave one shot per
# press (Coffin lock 1-3 never in play: switch flags 0x0020, as on 1.03); a light_all mode held every playfield
# insert in its colour on the LED view (the two sling skulls too, named -R/-G/-B on this build); a mode's own
# multiball (3, add-a-ball to 4, END on one ball left) and its ball save (saved drain served back, next drain
# ended the ball; the control ended on the first drain).
game           metallica_spike
version        1.04

