# ---- lamps: lamp <light ids R,G,B | one> <shot mask> <name> - read by lamp_map.py ----
# shot ties (PAD-306): this build has no cshot table, so the ties were made at the desk, as on Beatles 1.29, by name and by
# position: each switch's XY from the device table (class 1, the TestMode/metallica_playfield picture) against each
# insert's. A shot gets the insert in front of it (its arrow, its target's own light, its lane's light); the feature
# inserts in each lane (<lane> ELECTRIC CHAIR / SNAKE / GRAVE MARKER / HARDWIRED), the progress lights (ELECTRIC CHAIR 1-5,
# FUEL GAUGE, the E.O.L.s, GUITAR PICK), MULTIBALL, the UV lights, the flashers and the GI stay untied (0).
# Untied shots: Captive ball (0x400000, only UV decor near it) and Coffin lock 1-3 (their one light, COFFIN FLASH (X2),
# never shows on the insert boards, and the switches never fire in play).
# Emulator-proven 2026-10-01 (rig slot 3, muted, stock 1.04 card, PAD_NB_TRACE=1): the node bus decoded with
# leddecode.wide_decode_any against mode.log's clock. A light_shots ff00ff mode on every tied shot changed exactly the 32
# tied inserts to magenta (one-light ones to 255) in the 400 ms after START and handed them back at END; a light_shots
# 00ffff mode on 5 shots (Left loop, Rt ramp-left tgt, Left pop, Grave tgt-left, Left outlane) changed exactly
# LEFT LOOP ARROW, RIGHT RAMP TARGET-LEFT, LEFT POP, GRAVE LANE TARGET-L and LEFT OUTLANE. No other insert took the
# colour; the only other changes were the game's own blinkers. With the old untied lines the same mode logged
# "no insert of shots ... in this game's port" and held 0.
